<div dir=3D"ltr"><span></span></div>
<blockquote type=3D"cite">
<div dir=3D"ltr">


<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Good Morning,</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Unfortunately, I have no control of when the expert =
reports will be received.&nbsp; If we have a conference this week with the =
court I will ask the court=E2=80=99s attorney to inquire directly.&nbsp;
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">The supervision reports are generally benign.&nbsp; =
Factual and not overwhelming in any way.&nbsp; I am concerned about your cl=
ient=E2=80=99s reports about the visits and what is documented by the super=
visor.&nbsp; For example, Mr. Russell reports that Evie is
 constantly tired and hungry when he gets her but it is noted in the report=
 that he is the one trying to get the child to nap during the visit.&nbsp; =
Also, SS noted on March 31, 2019, that Mr. Russell fed Evie a few bits of b=
acon and sausage noting when he did that
 =E2=80=9CBM would not be happy about it=E2=80=9D.&nbsp; Yet he emailed tha=
t Evie accidentally ate a crumb of bacon that fell on his shirt which was o=
nly part of the story according to SS report.&nbsp; Also, Mr. Russell=E2=80=
=99s girlfriend Kelly=E2=80=99s insistence on being present when Evie arriv=
es
 and coming into the room during the visit gives me concern about your clie=
nt=E2=80=99s willingness to follow the rules.</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">With respect to SVE as supervisors, I never said tha=
t SVE was =E2=80=9Coverbooked=E2=80=9D those are your words not mine.&nbsp;=
 In fact, they do in fact have availability to schedule the visits during t=
he morning because most of their clients are older and
 require afternoon visits.&nbsp; SVE indicated that they wouldn=E2=80=99t a=
ccommodate four hour visits four days per week.&nbsp; However, one of the m=
ain concerns is that visits over two =E2=80=93 three consecutive hours are =
not recommended because they are difficult to supervise because
 the supervisor may need to leave the room to go to the bathroom which woul=
d leave the parent and the child unsupervised if even for a moment.&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">I would implore to include Tara in the nanny search =
from the beginning.&nbsp; Any search conducted unilaterally by Steve or any=
one on his behalf is going to be responded to with suspicion.&nbsp;
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Mr. Snyder=E2=80=99s email was inappropriate.&nbsp; =
There are way too many people involved in this matter giving their unsolici=
ted opinions.&nbsp; It is not helpful and while not tantamount to disruptin=
g the progress certainly created an unnecessary distraction.&nbsp;&nbsp;
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">With respect to =E2=80=9Cbruises=E2=80=9D, I advised=
 you that Tara reported to me that Evie returned from a visit with her fath=
er on Sunday, March 31 with a big bruise on her shin that was not there whe=
n she left for the visit.&nbsp; I told Ms. Walsh that it
 wasn=E2=80=99t unusual for a child Evie=E2=80=99s age to sustain bruises o=
n her legs now that she is walking.&nbsp; Ms. Walsh did not raise the issue=
 again.&nbsp; There is no =E2=80=9Cinjury=E2=80=9D to Evie=E2=80=99s neck.&=
nbsp; The child has a rash on her neck that is referred to as a =E2=80=9Cdr=
ool rash=E2=80=9D which you
 can imagine occurs when the child drools excessively and the saliva collec=
ts in the folds of the neck and causes irritation.&nbsp; This is not uncomm=
on in children of Evie=E2=80=99s age especially when teething.&nbsp; I beli=
eve that Ms. Walsh has responded to and treated this
 issue appropriately.&nbsp; As I stated, I have a release and have requeste=
d the child=E2=80=99s medical records but there is no indication that Evie =
is not being properly cared for.</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
