<div style=3D"border:none;border-top:solid #E1E1E1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in =
0in 0in">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><b>From:</b> Darren Enenstein &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:=
dse@enensteinlaw.com">dse@enensteinlaw.com</a>&gt;
<br>
<b>Sent:</b> Monday, April 15, 2019 10:52 PM<br>
<b>To:</b> Jennifer Jackman &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:jmj@mzw-law.com">jmj@mzw-=
law.com</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Cc:</b> Ruth Dayan Eget &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:rdeget@enensteinlaw.com">r=
deget@enensteinlaw.com</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Subject:</b> Russell Re Walsh/Evie Russell</p>
</div>
</div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<blockquote style=3D"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt">
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">Dear Jennifer,</span></p=
>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">Thank you for attending =
our call today. It was helpful in sharing solutions to help reunify Steve w=
ith his daughter and complete what has been a prolonged supervision process=
. Also it is my sincere hope that we
 can make progress in graduating Tara to her own home to decrease her level=
 of stress and bolster a sense of calm around little Evelyn Russell.&nbsp;A=
s discussed, my goals are obtaining a regular schedule for Steve and having=
 Steve graduate from the supervision
 requirement, especially in light of the positive supervisor reports which =
you have read. &nbsp;We both agreed the reports are positive. Knowing Steve=
, I am not surprised as he is very sweet when talking about his daughter an=
d only desire is to be around her on
 a regular basis. &nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">We also discussed the in=
itial differences between your requested supervisor company and that of Jas=
on Advocate=E2=80=99s recommendation towards the beginning of this case. Ho=
wever, in light of your recent conversation
 with SVE, a competing supervisor company, who is overbooked and cannot han=
dle 4 hour scheduled supervised visits, it seems prudent to stick with the =
current company. &nbsp;I did also see a prior email where you recommended t=
hat we the parties stick with the current
 supervising service. I don=E2=80=99t believe it is in the best interest of=
 Evie to rotate through more strangers in her life unless it is necessary o=
r it outweighs the potential harm, such as a neutral nanny. &nbsp;</span></=
p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">I appreciate your though=
ts about a neutral nanny and your interest in my idea of having a nurse Nan=
ny, a nanny with possibly some medical background. I shared this thought wi=
th my client and he also agreed that
 this could be a positive influence and promote continuity and increase saf=
ety for Evie Russell. &nbsp;Having a neutral Nanny will certainly help Tara=
, who is a first-time mother. &nbsp;Also, a neutral Nanny will help support=
 Tara to follow her stated desire to you of
 moving out of her parent=E2=80=99s home.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">We are starting a search=
 tomorrow of well respected nanny companies servicing Westchester County an=
d will provide identified candidates soon. Would you be available to meet w=
ith any of the recommended candidates?
 This could help promote and maintain a positive sense of neutrality.</span=
></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">We also discussed having=
 the experts submit their reports so that we could address removing the sup=
ervision order. It appears that Dr. Griffin and Dr. Hymowitz are ready to i=
ssue their report and therefore I would
 greatly appreciate your help and involvement in requesting that these repo=
rts be issued now.&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">Another issue we discuss=
ed was concerning communications with the supervisor and a concern on the p=
art of Tara=E2=80=99s new attorney, John Guttridge, about financial advisor=
 Sean Snyder sending a communication beyond
 his financial expertise. Specifically you mentioned that there was an emai=
l from Sean Snyder to the supervisor requesting that the interrupted visits=
 resume, if I recall correctly. &nbsp;I commented that such a comment on it=
s own is not tantamount to disrupting
 the progress of the case or somehow influencing parties in an adverse mann=
er. I do believe that Sean Snyder has communicated with the supervisor comp=
any regarding financial payments as that is his role. I am not aware of wri=
tten communications from girlfriend
 Kelly with the supervisor. I do believe that access to the supervisor comp=
any regarding communications is available.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black"><br>
<br>
</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">One important issue I wo=
uld like to probe further is the concerning injury around Evie=E2=80=99s ne=
ck. This was stated as a bruise and not a rash or something benign. Could y=
